;; status-enum — a claim's status must be one of the SHACL sh:in vocabulary
;; (REQ-KG-003 / REQ-KG-012).
;;
;; Booklogic port of the tbf:status sh:in constraint in assets/shapes.ttl:
;;   sh:path tbf:status ; sh:in ( "proposed" "verified" "disputed"
;;                                "superseded" "refuted" ) .
;;
;; A violation is a claim whose status equals NONE of the five vocabulary
;; values. The :filter ANDs five != clauses together, so the rule fires only
;; when status differs from every allowed value (an out-of-vocabulary status).
;; The compiler guards each comparison with !is_null, so a claim with a null
;; status is dropped rather than erroring (a missing status is the minCount
;; concern of a separate shape, not this one).
;;
;; MESSAGE NOTE: pyshacl auto-generates the sh:in message
;; ("Value ... not in ..."); EXACT pyshacl-message parity is a P2.3 concern.
;; The human message below is clear and stable for P2.2.
(defconstraint :status-enum
  :message "Claim status must be one of: proposed, verified, disputed, superseded, refuted."
  :path "https://example.org/book-knowledge#status"
  :component "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#InConstraintComponent"
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?focus]
          [?c :claim/status ?status]]
  :filter [[!= ?status "proposed"]
           [!= ?status "verified"]
           [!= ?status "disputed"]
           [!= ?status "superseded"]
           [!= ?status "refuted"]])
